{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Elohim made the beast of the earth after its kind, and the cattle after its kind, and every creeping thing of the ground.</b> Rather, man is the fourth creation, and this is what is written further on: ויהי האדם לנפש חיה (and man became a living soul)." "<b>[חיתו ארץ —</b> extra vav]."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The comment is terse; 'the fourth creation' refers to man being a distinct, separate act of creation on the sixth day."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:19:44.939916836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}